The S55 engine is the high-performance engine developed from the N55 by BMW M. It was introduced in the [[BMW_M3#F80_M3|F80 M3]] and [[BMW_M4#F82_M4|F82 M4]] replacing the [[BMW S65]] naturally aspirated V8 engine used in the previous generation M3 and was later used in the [[BMW M2#BMW M2 Competition|F87 M2 Competition/CS]].

Differences compared with the N55 include a closed-deck engine block, lightweight crankshaft, different crankshaft bearings, strengthened pistons/rods, different springs/valve material, twin turbos, twin fuel pumps, active exhaust, revised cooling system and intercoolers.<ref>{{cite web|title=F80 M3 / F82 M4 Complete Technical Docs (With S55 Engine Guide)|url=http://f80.bimmerpost.com/forums/showthread.php?t=1015603|website=Bimmerpost.com}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|title=Meet The New S55 Engine|url=http://www.bmwblog.com/2013/09/25/meet-new-s55-engine/|website=Bmwblog.com|date=25 September 2013 }}</ref>

